1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,890
Welcome to ClearClaim, a medical bill review project

2
00:00:03,890 --> 00:00:09,051
Complicated bills can leave patients unsure which charges to question

3
00:00:09,051 --> 00:00:15,933
ClearClaim organizes the bill, shows supporting evidence, and helps prepare a clear
response

4
00:00:15,933 --> 00:00:22,516
This walkthrough uses screenshots of the working public demo and fictional billing
data.

5
00:00:24,016 --> 00:00:28,480
Start by opening the Issues to find sample from the overview

6
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:34,357
The Evidence workspace places the original document beside editable charge rows

7
00:00:34,357 --> 00:00:39,564
Check the service, code, amount, quantity, and date against the source

8
00:00:39,564 --> 00:00:45,739
Correct missing or inaccurate fields before selecting Confirm charges and run audit

9
00:00:45,739 --> 00:00:49,236
Human review comes before the automated checks.

10
00:00:50,736 --> 00:01:01,528
The sample audit reports eight hundred and forty dollars billed, seven findings, and
a three hundred and forty dollar illustrative reduction

11
00:01:01,528 --> 00:01:09,776
Rules identify possible repeated charges, panel overlap, pricing differences, and
date or setting questions

12
00:01:09,776 --> 00:01:12,937
Overlapping amounts are not counted twice

13
00:01:12,937 --> 00:01:15,866
These figures use fictional references

14
00:01:15,866 --> 00:01:21,725
They do not establish fraud, patient responsibility, or a guaranteed refund.

15
00:01:23,225 --> 00:01:27,952
Open Findings and evidence to understand why a charge was flagged

16
00:01:27,952 --> 00:01:34,934
Here, an office visit costs two hundred dollars against a fictional one hundred
dollar reference

17
00:01:34,934 --> 00:01:40,752
The app shows the original charge, the comparison rule, and the source reference

18
00:01:40,752 --> 00:01:48,025
A useful next step is to ask the billing office for an itemized explanation and the
applicable rate.

19
00:01:49,525 --> 00:01:51,254
The user stays in control

20
00:01:51,254 --> 00:01:58,101
Record an assessment and add notes after checking the documents or speaking with the
billing office

21
00:01:58,101 --> 00:02:03,357
A repeated service may be legitimate, and a flag may reflect missing context

22
00:02:03,357 --> 00:02:10,826
Your assessment stays separate from the original audit so the evidence and your
interpretation remain clear.

23
00:02:12,326 --> 00:02:19,218
The Dispute letter tab turns selected findings into a draft request for clarification

24
00:02:19,218 --> 00:02:27,894
Choose which findings to include, select a tone, and edit the wording before
downloading a text or PDF copy

25
00:02:27,894 --> 00:02:32,596
The report also offers Excel, Markdown, and JSON downloads

26
00:02:32,596 --> 00:02:35,596
Review every export before sharing it

27
00:02:35,596 --> 00:02:41,515
ClearClaim helps prepare questions; it does not send a complaint for you.

28
00:02:43,015 --> 00:02:45,994
The public demo runs without API keys

29
00:02:45,994 --> 00:02:52,030
Your locally stored keys were not uploaded to GitHub or the hosting service

30
00:02:52,030 --> 00:02:56,779
Uploaded content and typed questions are not sent to an LLM

31
00:02:56,779 --> 00:03:03,701
On the hosted app, processing happens on the hosting server, not on the visitor
device

32
00:03:03,701 --> 00:03:05,552
Use synthetic data only

33
00:03:05,552 --> 00:03:08,209
Shared saved reviews are disabled

34
00:03:08,209 --> 00:03:15,775
Try the demo using the address on screen, and download your results before ending the
session.
